{"seq":43,"slug":"containers-orchestration","title":"容器与编排原理","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration","rating":{"composite":3.84,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 容器与编排原理\n\n把一段代码从开发者的笔记本搬到生产集群，中间横亘着「在我机器上能跑」这道经典鸿沟。容器技术用一套 Linux 内核原语把进程连同它的整个用户态环境打包成一个可移植单元，而编排系统则回答了下一个问题：当这样的单元从一个变成成千上万、跨越几百台机器时，谁来决定它们跑在哪、怎么联网、坏了怎么自愈。这个 hub 自底向上地拆解这两层，让你既懂得一个容器在内核里到底是什么，也懂得 Kubernetes 这类系统为什么长成今天的样子。\n\n整个 hub 由四章组成，刻意按「抽象层从低到高」排列，每一章都建立在前一章的结论之上。\n\n第一章「基础」回答最根本的问题：容器到底是什么。它先用对比的方式讲清容器相对虚拟机的价值取向，再深入 Linux 命名空间与 cgroups 这两组内核机制——前者负责「看不见」，后者负责「用不超」，二者合起来就是隔离的全部秘密。最后落到镜像与 OCI 标准，解释那个可移植单元在磁盘上和仓库里的真实形态。读完这一章，你对「容器」一词不再有任何魔法成分。\n\n第二章「运行时」把镜像变成跑起来的进程。它讲清楚从 kubelet 到 containerd 再到 runc 的调用链，讲清楚容器之间和容器与外界如何联网，以及容器里写下的数据如何在重启后幸存。这一章是单机视角的终点：它假设你只有一台主机，把容器跑通、连通、存住。\n\n第三章「编排」把视角拉升到集群。Kubernetes 的架构、调度器如何把 Pod 放到合适的节点、以及 Deployment 这类控制器如何用「声明期望、持续逼近」的协调循环维持系统状态——这三篇构成了编排的核心心智模型。它复用了前两章对运行时和网络的理解，但关注点完全转向了分布式协调。\n\n第四章「生产实践」面对真实世界的运营压力。服务如何被发现、流量如何从集群外进来、多租户下如何收紧权限与隔离爆炸半径、以及当几千个容器同时运行时如何观测它们的健康。这一章把前三章的原理放进生产环境的约束里检验，是从「能跑」到「敢上线」的最后一跃。\n\n四章读下来是一条完整的因果链：内核原语决定了容器的能力边界，运行时把这些能力编排成可用的进程，集群编排把单机能力放大到规模，生产实践再为规模套上安全与可观测的护栏。建议按顺序阅读；若你只想补某一环，每篇文档都会在引用其它篇主讲的概念处给出交叉链接，方便你顺藤摸瓜。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"containerization-overview","title":"容器化概念与价值","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/foundations/containerization-overview"},{"seq":2,"slug":"linux-primitives","title":"Linux 命名空间与 cgroups","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/foundations/linux-primitives"},{"seq":3,"slug":"images-oci","title":"镜像与 OCI 标准","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/foundations/images-oci"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"runtime","title":"运行时","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/runtime","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"container-runtimes","title":"容器运行时","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/runtime/container-runtimes"},{"seq":2,"slug":"networking","title":"容器网络","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/runtime/networking"},{"seq":3,"slug":"storage-volumes","title":"存储与卷","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/runtime/storage-volumes"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"orchestration","title":"编排","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/orchestration","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"kubernetes-architecture","title":"Kubernetes 架构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/orchestration/kubernetes-architecture"},{"seq":2,"slug":"scheduling-resources","title":"调度与资源管理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/orchestration/scheduling-resources"},{"seq":3,"slug":"workloads-controllers","title":"工作负载与控制器","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/orchestration/workloads-controllers"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"production","title":"生产实践","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/production","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"service-discovery-ingress","title":"服务发现与 Ingress","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/production/service-discovery-ingress"},{"seq":2,"slug":"security-isolation","title":"安全与隔离","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/production/security-isolation"},{"seq":3,"slug":"observability-ops","title":"可观测性与运维","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/containers-orchestration/production/observability-ops"}]}]}